35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The post-occupancy reviews show that spaces are rated highest when anyone can book them.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The timetable records show that every room taken out of service requires hired space off-site.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The tender records show mechanical lots rising by a fifth, while surfacing held steady.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The renewal reserve for audiovisual kit was never opened, so we have no money for replacements.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The staffing posts show front-of-house roles are unfilled, but technicians have spare hours.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, if we have to hire off-site space, that adds a lot of cost and disruption.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, exactly. And the booking data shows specialist rooms are idle, but general rooms are full.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, if we don't have a reserve, we are stuck paying for old equipment out of current budgets.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, yes. And the delivery schedules show that comfort-based projects slip, but inspection ones don't.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, the technicians are doing manual checks because the equipment can't do it alone.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,We should prioritize projects that have broad access and high user satisfaction.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,We need to minimize the time rooms are out of service to avoid hiring off-site space.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,We should avoid projects with high mechanical costs that are rising rapidly.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"We need to ensure we have a plan for replacing equipment, not just buying it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,We should consider projects that reduce the manual workload on the technicians.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,The data suggests that general-purpose spaces are more valuable than specialist ones.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,The cost of downtime is significant and should be a major factor in our decision.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,The rising cost of mechanical work makes some options less attractive.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,The lack of a renewal reserve is a serious gap in our planning.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,The current staffing model is unsustainable and needs to be addressed.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
