60,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Candidate A, the Central Study Commons, fits the high-usage, general-access model we want.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Candidate A also has a short construction timeline, which minimizes downtime costs.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate A avoids the high-cost mechanical work that is rising in price.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate A includes a service desk, which can help manage the space and reduce manual checks.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Candidate A reduces the need for manual upkeep compared to the other options.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, I agree. The booking data supports the idea that general spaces are more useful.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, yes. And the timetable records show that shorter projects are better for us.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the service desk is a good idea. It can help with the renewal reserve issue too.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, exactly. It gives us a place to manage the equipment and plan for replacements.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, the reduced manual workload is a big plus for the technicians.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I think Candidate A is the best choice for us.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
